    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. When you mention \"displacement\" or the \"gentrification index,\" I'm curious about the demographic side of things. In your experience analyzing these trends, how much do shifts in the racial or ethnic makeup of a neighborhood serve as a reliable predictor for economic instability or a decline in property values? Is there a way to factor those cultural shifts into a risk model without being arbitrary?",
